## My recommendation: one important production decision

Do not begin by building all the animations.

First, create one exceptionally good character model and render it in three situations:

1. Neutral daylight portrait.
2. Residential streetlight close-up.
3. Walking full-body shot at night.

If the character does not look convincing in these three tests, we should fix the model before investing time in animation.

Phase 1 is complete only when we have a character worth putting in a cinematic.

After that, Phase 2 should be the residential street itself, with the same The Last of Us standard for environmental detail, lighting, materials and atmosphere.